  "slug": "high-nanoantenna-b3b2",
  "summary": "Recent preprints demonstrate reversible tuning of BIC resonances by vapor anion exchange and liquid-crystal integration.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is engineering resonant response in metasurfaces through mode coupling and environment. Two items address quasi-bound states in the continuum (quasi-BICs): a MAPbBr3 perovskite metasurface whose BIC resonances shift reversibly and continuously under HCl/HBr vapor anion exchange, and a symmetric silicon metasurface in a nematic liquid crystal whose anisotropy-induced quasi-BICs are actively tunable. A third reports polarization-independent self-hybridized strong coupling between Brillouin-zone-folding quasi-BICs and A excitons in bulk WS2 metasurfaces. The NbOCl2 study of room-temperature antiferroelectricity is a materials result outside the resonant-nanostructure thread. What is new is reversible, continuous spectral control via chemical exchange and liquid-crystal integration, alongside excitonic strong coupling in bulk material. All four are preprints.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-25"
}
